<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal details 1997 budget package.</title>
<headline>Portugal details 1997 budget package.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government on Tuesday sent its 1997 budget plan to parliament, detailing how it intends to cut the deficit to 2.9 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) next year from 4.0 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>The budget document saw the deficit totalling 508.8 billion escudos in 1997 against 659.5 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said in the budget document, the broad outlines of which had already been published, that the reduction reflected a projected increase in government receipts of 0.8 percent of GDP and a fall in current spending of 0.3 percent.</p>
<p>The following is a table of government projected spending and receipts in billions of escudos:</p>
<p>			   Estimate	Budget	1996     1997</p>
<p>			    1996	    1997	    Pct of GDP</p>
<p>Current receipts     6,906.3	7,495.5	41.6     42.4</p>
<p>(of which tax and  social contribs     5,374.5	5,790.5	32.4     32.8</p>
<p> Current spending     6,968.6	7,376.6	42.0     41.7</p>
<p> Current balance	  -62.3	  118.9	-0.4	0.7</p>
<p> Capital receipts	 541.0	  623.2	 3.3	3.5</p>
<p> Capital spending     1,138.2	1.250.9	 6.9	7.1</p>
<p> Capital balance	 -597.2	 -627.7	-3.6     -3.6</p>
<p> Total receipts	 7,447.3	8,118.7	44.8     45.9</p>
<p> Total spending	 8,106.8	8,627.5	48.8     48.8</p>
<p> Primary balance	  141.3	  267.9	 0.9	1.5</p>
<p> Budget deficit	  -659.5	 -508.8	-4.0     -2.9</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 351103150035</p>
</text>
